OL,3,GNEWSATrain announcements too loud, say
OL,4,Aneighbours
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople living near a new city railway
OL,7,Fstation said platform announcements
OL,8,Fwere so loud it had ruined the "peace
OL,9,Fand calm" of their gardens and
OL,10,Fallotments.
OL,12,FCambridge South opened to passengers at
OL,13,Fthe end of June, linking Addenbrooke's
OL,14,FHospital, the biomedical campus and
OL,15,FTrumpington to the rail network.
OL,17,FWhile it has the capacity to welcome
OL,18,F1.8 million passengers annually, those
OL,19,Fliving nearby said they did not need to
OL,20,Fknow when and "where the next train is
OL,21,Fgoing to" from the station speakers.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,374,370,200,160,0,100
